  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Доктор, а что с ним?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Doctor, what is wrong with him?' Eleonora anchors the line on 'Doctor', while 'him' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Обследование покажет точнее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The examination will show more precisely.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'medical examination' and finishing on 'more precisely'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Распространённый случай, всему виной переедание.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'A common case, overeating is to blame for everything.' Notice how Russian expresses 'common' and 'overeating' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Нужно себя сдерживать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'One must restrain oneself.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'needed' before landing on 'to restrain'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Вы, кстати, тоже имейте в виду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You, by the way, should keep that in mind too.' The meaning hinges on 'you' working together with 'mind' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Префекта до инфаркта довёл!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You drove the prefect to a heart attack!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'prefect' and finishing on 'drove'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Рисковать человеческой жизнью ради победы!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Risking a human life for the sake of a victory!' Eleonora brings out the contrast between 'to risk' and 'human' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Пари продолжается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The wager continues.' In Russian, the idea of 'bet' flows naturally into 'continues' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Это вам, Михаил Джекович.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
